      "directNodeIds": [
        "math:sum-difference-cubes"
      ],
      "explanation": "The expression requires \\(a\\ne0\\). Since \\(a^{-3}=(1/a)^3\\), it is a difference of two cubes. Use\n\\[\nu^3-v^3=(u-v)(u^2+uv+v^2)\n\\]\nwith \\(u=a\\) and \\(v=1/a\\). Their product is \\(uv=1\\), so\n\\[\na^3-a^{-3}\n=\\left(a-\\frac1a\\right)\n\\left(a^2+1+\\frac1{a^2}\\right).\n\\]\nThis identity holds for every \\(a\\ne0\\), giving choice A.",
      "id": "difference-of-cubes",
